    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="0812" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Takahira.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the telegram, dated the 4th instant, from Baron Komura to you, in which he
                    announces the death of Mr. Alfred E. Buck, United States minister to Japan, and
                    expresses the condolence of the Japanese Government at the sad event.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to say that the Government of the United States greatly
                    appreciates the courtesy and sympathy of the Japanese Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
